  "published": "2026-06-04T23:52:04.88Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0-preview.7: Continues the preview.6 fail-closed hardening pass with one targeted security fix. SECURITY: a JOSE header whose JSON had duplicate property names (e.g. two \"enc\" or \"typ\" entries — non-interoperable per RFC 8259 §4 and forbidden by RFC 7515 §4) was triggering ArgumentException out of System.Text.Json's lazy dictionary materialization, which escaped Validate as an unsealed exception type instead of the documented PqJwtValidationException — a fail-closed totality violation. The header parser now wraps the duplicate-key case as PqJwtValidationException(MalformedJson); pinned by a regression test. Surfaced by the Tier 2 coverage-guided fuzz target (fuzz/PostQuantum.Jwt.Fuzz, SharpFuzz + libFuzzer) on its first operational run — a complement to the random-input PqJwtFuzzTests shipped in preview.6. Tokens produced by this library's builder are unaffected; the public API and wire format are unchanged. Production-oriented preview: NOT independently audited, NOT a drop-in OAuth/OIDC/JWT replacement. Full notes: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-jwt/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md — known limitations: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-jwt/blob/main/KNOWN-GAPS.md.",
